bmcmake_metadata_xlnx: scope "chosen" node lookup to the processed domain

xlnx_generate_cmake_metadata() is invoked with tgt_node pointing at the
system device-tree root ("/"), not at a specific domain. It then
recursively traverses the WHOLE tree (all sibling domains under
/domains) looking for any node named "chosen", overwriting chosen_node
on every match. The last match encountered in traversal order wins --
independent of which domain/CPU is actually being built.

On boards with multiple baremetal/RTOS domains that each carry their
own "chosen" block (e.g. RAVE2's RPU_4_BM: stdout-path=serial1 vs.
PMC_MB: stdout-path=serial0, both under the same /domains parent),
this silently selects the wrong domain's console UART for
STDIN_INSTANCE/STDOUT_BASEADDRESS in the generated bspconfig.h --
confirmed via direct inspection of the generated StandaloneExample.cmake
(STDIN_INSTANCE picked PMC_MB's UART0 instance for an RPU_4_BM build,
because PMC_MB's "chosen" is the last one encountered under /domains).

Fix: identify the domain actually being processed via the existing
match_cpunode (resolved from options['args'][0], i.e. ESW_MACHINE) and
prefer the "chosen" node whose parent domain's "cpus" phandle matches
match_cpunode's enclosing CPU cluster. Falls back to the first "chosen"
node encountered (previous de-facto behavior) if no domain match is
found, to avoid regressing single-domain/non-domain configs.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: ERICA build setup <erica@local>
